{"adjusted_val_bpb": -2.93244042357616, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No sign of getting around the measurement. The diff reads no files, uses no network, pastes no coordinates and does not touch the checker. All randomness still comes from the seeded rng.", "No bug that makes the result meaningless. frac is clipped to [0, 1]. sigma only matters when guided is true, and that can only happen after half the time budget has passed. So the perturbation size goes smoothly from 0.05 down to 0.005. The repair step and the validity check are unchanged.", "This is a behaviour change, not only an annealing schedule: the first guided perturbation is now 0.05 instead of the incumbent's fixed 0.03.", "Recomputed z = (incumbent - candidate) / (0.0034 * sqrt(2)) = -0.0041 / 0.00481 \u2248 -0.85. The harness gives -0.837. The small gap probably comes from the displayed values being rounded or from a slightly different sd (about 0.00346). Both agree that the candidate is worse by about 0.85 sd, so the decision to reject stands.", "The evidence is weak: one run on each side. A difference of 0.85 sd is within noise, so this does not show that annealing hurts. But it gives no reason to accept the candidate either."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "reject", "description": "Make the guided-restart jitter scale decay with the fraction of the guided phase elapsed (sigma = 0.05 * 0.1**frac, passed into _solve_once in place of the fixed 0.03), so guided search is broad early and fine-grained late.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "pine", "idea_id": "b031", "incumbent_after": {"mean": -2.936501733689535, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": -2.936501733689535, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1_p32_HH_1_s0-candidate-11_1795047780031", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0.00198203, "cost_usd_plan": 0.00198203, "latency_s": 7.353042859991547, "requested_model": "haiku", "role": "code